---
title: "Add live planning pool items"
pr: 96
module: acme_planning
---

{% section id="m-pool" navLabel="planning_pool_item.py" icon="database" group="Models" title="planning.pool.item — the derived lens" %}

A read-only SQL view (`_auto = False`) over active converted allocations. Each pool item keeps allocation grain and exposes **total**, **placed**, and **remaining** charge. No new table, no second copy of the charge.

{% diff file="addons/acme_planning/models/planning_pool_item.py" from=1 to=62 /%}

{% fields %}
{% field name="allocation_id" type="Many2one → planning.allocation" %}
The link back to the source allocation. One pool item per allocation.
{% /field %}
{% field name="total_hours" type="Float (view column)" %}
Read straight from the allocation; never stored on the pool item.
{% /field %}
{% field name="placed_hours" type="Float (computed)" %}
Summed hours of every non-cancelled slot pointing at the allocation.
{% /field %}
{% field name="remaining_hours" type="Float (computed)" %}
Always `max(total − placed, 0)`; never negative, never decremented.
{% /field %}
{% /fields %}

{% method sig="_planning_placed_hours_by_id(self) -> Dict[int, float]" decorator="@api.depends('slot_ids.state')" %}
Sums the hours of non-cancelled slots per allocation, one query for the whole recordset. Callers read the dict instead of looping per record.
{% /method %}

{% method sig="init(self)" %}
Drops and recreates the SQL view with `CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW`. The `WHERE` clause keeps only rows with state = 'converted' and an active project.
{% /method %}

{% diff file="addons/acme_planning/security/ir.model.access.csv" from=1 to=4 mark="3" /%}

{% callout tone="warn" %}
The view is read-only but the ACL still matters: without the read line in `ir.model.access.csv`, the smart button raises an access error for plain planners. Check the group on line 3 is `planning.group_planning_user`, not manager.
{% /callout %}

{% /section %}
